      ],
      "sha256": "1ce5640ca8653f1ed1ff6d9fa5e06b65fe9d2df514dd253a6e289a2dc5aef543",
      "kind": "figure",
      "alt": "Figure 6: A screenshot of a rectangular computer window. The window has 2 sections, each one having rows of speech utterances on the left, YouTube video clips in the center, and Fusion 360 command names on the right. Each section has a gray background."
    },
    {
      "path": "figures/krosnick-think-aloud-computing-chi2021/figure-007-p008.png",
      "node": "887:0",
      "page": 8,
      "bbox": [
        315.9549865722656,
        81.68916320800781,
        562.4423828125,
        248.32199096679688
      ],
      "sha256": "8f514051bd676b69b0d92d6ab15af1137481af3adeb8f9733df4f1ca95f2e881",
      "kind": "figure",
      "alt": "Figure 7: A system diagram, with arrows connecting components. On the left is a speaking head representing the user. To the right an arrow points to a computer monitor/webpage icon representing the think-aloud system. The think-aloud system component then has arrows pointing to the right, sending speech to the Azure cloud (cloud icon) and livestream to YouTube (play button icon). The Azure cloud has an arrow pointing to the left back to the think-aloud system sending transcript. The YouTube icon has an arrow pointing to the left back to the think-aloud system sending playback. In the far right column are the 3rd party applications section, specifically Fusion 360, which sends an arrow to the left to the think-aloud system with command metadata. Below Fusion 360 is the OSX operating system with a Mac smiley face icon, with an arrow to the left to think-aloud system sending accessibility information."
    },
    {
      "path": "figures/krosnick-think-aloud-computing-chi2021/figure-008-p009.png",
      "node": "891:0",
      "page": 9,
      "bbox": [
        51.7979736328125,
        81.68604278564453,
        563.5382690429688,
        194.16195678710938
      ],
      "sha256": "648cd6b2617cd7948470955621bc0da765e240fb39c6c68259a5ba234910d096",
      "kind": "figure",
      "alt": "Figure 8 is a chart illustrating participants' ratings of how much effort it took to document knowledge for think-aloud and traditional documentation techniques. The chart has 2 mini bar charts. On the left is the bar chart for the think-aloud condition. It has 3 bars, from left: a red bar of height 3 (i.e., 3 participants out of 12) for the category of \"high effort\", a yellow bar of height 3 for \"medium effort\", and a green bar of height 6 for \"low effort\". On the right is the bar chart for the traditional documentation condition. It has 3 bars, from left: a red bar of height 4 for the \"high effort\", a yellow bar of height 2 for \"medium effort\", and a green bar of height 6 for \"low effort\". Note that these categories are aggregations of the participant ratings from the 7-point Likert scale results (between 1-Very Low Effort, and 7-Very High Effort). Ratings (1, 2, 3) have been aggregated into \"low effort\", rating (4) is \"medium effort\", and ratings (5, 6, 7) have been aggregated into \"high effort\"."
    }
